   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "תִּינוֹקֶת שֶׁהֵבִיאָה כּוּ׳. אָמַר רַבִּי אֲבָהוּ אָמַר רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר: הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי יְהוּדָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «A young girl who» reached the age of puberty and «grew» two pubic hairs can no longer perform refusal to end a marriage with a husband to whom she was married as a minor by her mother and brothers after her father’s death. Rabbi Yehuda maintains that she retains the right of refusal until the pubic hair grows to the extent that the black hair is preponderant in the pubic area. «Rabbi Abbahu says» that «Rabbi Elazar says:» The «halakha» is «in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda.»"
  }
 ],
